# BOOTSTRAPME — automated machine setup for an agent

You are an agent on a fresh machine. This repo (pi-rs) has just been cloned.
Your job: make the project fully operational, including the differential
parity suite. Work through the steps below **in order**. Each step tells you
how to check whether it is already done — skip completed steps (idempotent).

Repo layout note: the patch file referenced in step 3 lives in this repo at
`parity/ts-repo/lexmarkdown-seam.patch` (relative to the pi-rs repo root —
your current working directory should be that root).

## Step 0 — Verify this repo

- Confirm `Cargo.toml`, `crates/`, `parity/`, `parity/ts-repo/lexmarkdown-seam.patch`
  all exist. If not, you are not in the pi-rs repo root; `cd` there first.

## Step 1 — Toolchain

Check, and install if missing:

- **Rust**: `rustc --version` (developed on 1.97.x). If missing or older than
  that, install via <https://rustup.rs> (stable toolchain is fine).
- **Node.js 24**: `node --version` must report v24.x — the parity TS harness
  imports the original repo's TUI `.ts` source directly via Node 24
  type-stripping. If missing/wrong major version, install Node 24
  (e.g. via nvm: `nvm install 24`, or nodesource, or your package manager).

## Step 2 — Clone the original pi (TypeScript) repo

The parity harness expects it at `/tmp/pi-repo` (the defaults for `PI_DIST`,
`PI_TUI_SRC` assume this path). Only clone if absent:

```bash
test -d /tmp/pi-repo/.git || git clone https://github.com/earendil-works/pi /tmp/pi-repo
cd /tmp/pi-repo
git fetch origin
git checkout --detach 698a2d2   # the commit the parity suite was developed against
```

If `/tmp/pi-repo` exists but is on a different commit, `git checkout --detach
698a2d2` anyway. Do NOT `git pull`/update past this commit — parity results
are only guaranteed against it.

## Step 3 — Apply the lexMarkdown test-seam patch

`parity/ts-repo/lexmarkdown-seam.patch` adds a `lexMarkdown()` export to the
original repo's `packages/tui/src/components/markdown.ts`. It is a test seam
(required by the Rust port's marked-lexer differential tests) that exists
nowhere upstream — this patch file is the only durable copy.

```bash
cd /tmp/pi-repo
git apply /ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/pi-rs/parity/ts-repo/lexmarkdown-seam.patch
```

Idempotency: first run `git status --short -- packages/tui/src/components/markdown.ts`.
If it already shows the file as modified, the patch is applied — skip.
If `git apply` fails, check `git diff` — the seam may already be present
(look for `export function lexMarkdown`); only apply if it is missing.

Leave the change uncommitted in `/tmp/pi-repo` (a pristine checkout is what
the patch targets; committing it locally is also acceptable but unnecessary).

## Step 4 — Install deps and build the original repo

The TS harness runs the **built dist** at
`/tmp/pi-repo/packages/coding-agent/dist/index.js`, which is not in git:

```bash
cd /tmp/pi-repo
npm install
npm run build
```

(`npm run build` compiles all workspaces in dependency order.) Idempotency:
skip `npm run build` if `packages/coding-agent/dist/index.js` already exists
and `packages/tui/src/components/markdown.ts`'s mtime predates the dist —
when in doubt, rebuild; it is safe to rerun.

## Step 5 — Build and test this repo

From the pi-rs repo root:

```bash
cargo build
cargo test
```

## Step 6 — Run the parity suite (end-to-end verification)

```bash
cd /path/to/pi-rs/parity
node run-parity.mjs
```

Success criteria: all cases pass (the repo's README/TRACKING.md record the
current case count; 239+ cases as of the last update). If markdown-lexer
cases fail, re-check step 3 (missing seam) and step 1 (Node < 24).

## Troubleshooting / notes

- **Env overrides**: if the original repo is NOT at `/tmp/pi-repo`, export
  `PI_DIST=<repo>/packages/coding-agent/dist/index.js` and
  `PI_TUI_SRC=<repo>/packages/tui/src/utils.ts` before running parity.
- **`~/.pi/agent/bin`** (fd, rg): auto-downloaded by the pi agent at runtime;
  no action needed.
- Push remote for this repo is the `Shitnobi/pi-rs` fork (see `MIGRATION.md`
  for human-oriented background).
- Do not modify anything inside `/tmp/pi-repo` beyond step 3's patch.
